Package: theoceansclock
Title: What Tells a Coral Reef That Tonight Is the Night?
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mihael", "Atanasov", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Pirasanna", "Siva", role = "aut"))
Description: A research compendium, not an installable package. It joins historical
    coral spawning records with NOAA regional heat stress, NASA Moon positions,
    an aquarium diary and a tank experiment, then tests how spawning fits the
    yearly, lunar and daily cycles of the ocean. Run run.R from the project root.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    ggplot2,
    jsonlite,
    patchwork,
    pdftools,
    ragg,
    readr,
    readxl,
    scales,
    sf,
    svglite,
    systemfonts,
    tibble,
    tidyr
